  <p class="standfirst">There is no single number, and this page will not invent one. What follows is every absolute figure for producing brand content that could be read directly off the surface publishing it, each one dated, with its method beside it and the disagreements left in rather than averaged out.</p>

  <h2>What does brand content production cost in 2026?</h2>

  <p>Between about $0.25 for one bulk image edit and $372,000 committed for a year of a dedicated creative team. The spread is that wide because those are different units, not different prices for the same thing. hubStudio compiled the bands below from published surfaces, one card at a time, and averaged none of them.</p>

  <p>One scope note before the table. This page prices the making of an asset: capture, retouch, layout, edit, generation, the words. It does not price media, creator sponsorship fees, or the monthly retainers sold under the name content marketing, all three of which dominate the search results for this question and measure something else entirely. Every figure below was re-read at source on 17 September 2026.</p>

