  <p>That second-to-last row is worth dwelling on, because it is the comparison every budget holder wants and the one this page will not make. Fifty dollars an hour and $54.32 an hour are close enough to look like a verdict. They are not the same hour. One of them is sold with a cap on concurrent work and no camera in the building; the other is employed, and what share of it is productive is a number no source publishes in any market.</p>

